  {"id":"2Esd","name":"2 Esdras","chapters":16,"testament":"OT","beyond":{"canons":["orthodox","ethiopian","anglican"],"text":"web","note":"Called 4 Esdras in the Latin Vulgate and 3 Esdras in Slavonic Orthodox Bibles, which include it. Chapters 3–14 are the Jewish apocalypse known as 4 Ezra, which the Ethiopian church reads as Ezra Sutuel; chapters 1–2 and 15–16 are later Christian additions."}},
  {"id":"1En","name":"1 Enoch","chapters":108,"testament":"OT","beyond":{"canons":["ethiopian"],"text":"charles-enoch","note":"R. H. Charles printed chapter 92 first, then 91:1–11 and 18–19, then 93, then 91:12–17, the order he judged original; the reader keeps the chapters in their usual order."}},
  {"id":"Jub","name":"Jubilees","chapters":50,"testament":"OT","beyond":{"canons":["ethiopian"],"text":"charles-jubilees","note":"The transcription of Charles this text comes from has no verse numbers; CrossWire's editor added them. Checked against the margin numbers of Charles's 1913 printing, they agree in most chapters but run one behind his in parts of about a dozen (1:26 here is his 1:27), where two of his verses were run together."}},
